    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.41), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against the left-handed Kay. **Trea Turner** remains our premier engine; his ability to exploit the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile combined with his elite sprint speed makes him the primary catalyst in our pursuit of stolen bases. **Christian Yelich** (74.32) is also a standout play, as he draws a +14% park boost and a slow delivery from Feltner, creating an ideal environment for him to pad our counting stats. **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.80) are both strong starts today, as they benefit from wind-aided conditions that elevate their power ceilings despite varying platoon constraints.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Colt Keith** (48.48), who hovered near our threshold but ultimately yielded to our starters due to a lower projected efficiency against Woo. While **Colt Keith** possesses solid underlying metrics, the lineup concentration of our active starters\u2014specifically those batting at the top of the order like **Casey Schmitt** (63.20)\u2014provided higher floor stability for this afternoon\u2019s 5x5 targets. We are monitoring **Junior Caminero** (54.47) closely; although he is a high-upside asset, his score is currently suppressed by a -19% penalty against the elite secondary stuff of Gusto. We remain clear of the basement today, though we are keeping **Dillon Dingler** (38.53) on ice as he falls below our 40.0 efficiency floor, and we continue to track the minor league status of **Rece Hinds** to ensure no roster gaps emerge as we manage our remaining game caps.",
